    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2DsBzZu2upUckxWhTEYCcSG)_\n\nFirst implementation of the design in `docs/architecture/citation-matching-from-selection.org`, macOS only, for testing.\n\n## What is in it\n- `sp-cite-match` (`docs/tangles/academic/sp-cite-match.org`):\n  - normalises text and BibTeX fields (accents, casing, ligatures, line-end hyphens);\n  - scores surname, year, title and journal, with a DOI shortcut; returns `accept`, `ambiguous` or `none`;\n  - splits a selected Bibliography into entries;\n  - writes a `Cited works` section between markers (idempotent, shows which works have litnotes);\n  - `org-protocol://sp-cite-match?file=NAME` handler.\n- `sp-reading` (`docs/tangles/academic/sp-reading.org`): citekey to DEVONthink record, open at a page, or index the PDF / open in Preview.\n- `hammerspoon/.config/hammerspoon/cite-match.lua`: hotkey (Ctrl+Shift+K) that copies the selection and calls `emacsclient`; loaded from `init.lua` inside a `pcall`.\n- ERT tests: `tests/sp-cite-match-test.el` (12), `tests/sp-reading-test.el` (7); all pass on Emacs 29.3 in batch.\n\n## Not tested (please try on the Mac)\n- Everything against the real `.bib` files and vault; the score thresholds are guesses.\n- The AppleScript in `sp-reading` (search, `index path ... to`, bulk `uuid of every item`) was written from memory of the dictionary. The module doc lists what to check by hand first.\n- The litnote lookup through `citar-has-notes` / `citar-get-notes` with `citar-vulpea`.\n- `emacsclient` path, `org-protocol` handling and the Hammerspoon file were not run (no Lua or macOS here).\n\n## Not built yet\nLinux script, DEVONthink selection/UUID return, item-link backfill. No CHANGELOG edits.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCcNep549ieuxU71WK)_",
